35,2,1,talk,May,,The tally shows two people use it eleven times. The fridge was cleared twice by one person.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The wall is thin plasterboard. I can hear everything. Also, crumbs are under three keyboards.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Servas,,Eleven callouts for equipment. The store room had none. The tally confirms the heavy users.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"We paid 68,000 yen for nine bookings. The meeting room fit-out is 141,000 yen. The kitchen is 96,000.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,The last awkward talk was in front of everyone. Unplanned talk is only by the printer now.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,May,,"@Sakura, 141,000 is a lot. But if we book it, we stop the mess.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Servas, if the wall is thin, a quiet room is impossible. We need soundproofing or a different use.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Misaki, a quiet room requires silence. The wall fails that. A meeting space might work if booked.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@May, the kitchen is cheaper. But who cleans the crumbs? The invoices show we pay for space, not cleaning.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Misaki, if we have a meeting space, can we have private talks? The printer is not private.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,May,,"@Kenji, a meeting space with a calendar means we know who is there. No more guessing.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Sakura, the kitchen quote includes a fridge. But the old fridge was a mess. Who maintains it?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@May, the tally shows heavy use. A meeting space fits the demand. A quiet room does not.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"@Servas, the meeting space is more expensive. But the invoices show we are already paying for hourly hire.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@May, I agree. A meeting space gives us a place to talk without the whole office listening.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,May,,I am leaning towards the meeting space. It solves the usage and the privacy issue.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"The wall is the problem. A meeting space with a screen might help focus, but the noise remains.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Servas,,The hours go to upkeep. A meeting space with a calendar reduces the unplanned mess.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Sakura,,The figures show the meeting space is an investment. The kitchen is cheaper but messier.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Kenji,,I vote for the meeting space. It gives us a place to connect without the awkwardness.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
